  "mett.focus.summon.standing": "You have no standing with %s.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_FOCUS_BEDROCK.1": "Bedrock is the one stone the world is built on. Given enough entropy, and enough Vis, even that can be unbound - though never at the very floor of the world, where the void begins.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_FOCUS_SUMMON.1": "A focus of summoning calls one soldier of a people to your side. Only those who hold standing with that people may call, and only the sworn may call their elites.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_JARS.1": "Essentia is bulky, and the roads of Middle-earth are long. Compressing a jar's contents lets a single vessel carry far more of one aspect, at the cost of weaker suction.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_RING.1": "A ring of mithril washed in sanity soap turns aside the whisper of the Shadow. Its wearer spends less Vis on every cast, and carries less warp for it.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_ROOT.1": "The Free Peoples and the Shadow both work Vis, and each shapes it in its own tongue. Where a Thaumaturge reaches for a primal, a captain of Gondor reaches for the loyalty of the men beside him. The two arts answer to the same currents.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_STORAGE.1": "Gulduril, ithildin, edhelmir and their kin are metals that hold more than their weight in light. Stored in blocks they glow, and a stared mithril block shines like a small star.",
  "mett.research_page.METT_WANDS.1": "A rod bound with a faction's own metal draws on the standing its bearer holds with that people: kin of the faction feed it swiftly, a friendly folk slowly, and a hostile one not at all. Caps work as they always have - the rarer the metal, the cheaper the cast.",
  "mett.tooltip.ring_warpward": "Vis cost %s%% lower, warp %s lower while worn",
  "tc.research_name.METT": "Middle-earth Thaumaturgy",
  "tc.research_text.METT": "Vis in the Third Age"
}
